Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.
Question: Based on the following merger agreement excerpt, is the provision affecting the ability to consummate the transaction subject to carveouts for specified adverse events?
Option A: No
Option B: Yes

Merger Agreement Excerpt: 
"Material Adverse Impact" means any change, event, circumstance or condition that, either individually or in aggregation with other similar events, would (i) prevent, materially delay or materially impair the ability of the Acquiring Party to consummate the transactions contemplated by this Agreement, or (ii) have a material adverse effect on the overall financial or operational condition of the Acquiring Party. Notwithstanding the foregoing, no Material Adverse Impact shall be deemed to have occurred to the extent that such change, event, circumstance or condition arises directly after the execution of this Agreement from any of the following: 
(a) general fluctuations in global or domestic economic conditions, including changes in interest rates, inflation rates or currency exchange rates; 
(b) routine adjustments required by newly adopted or amended regulatory or accounting standards; 
(c) force majeure events, including natural disasters, pandemics or geopolitical disturbances not unique to the operations of the Acquiring Party; 
(d) changes in market sentiment or the public announcement of this Agreement. 
For the purposes of this definition, any event that would otherwise hinder the ability of the Acquiring Party to consummate the transactions is subject to the foregoing carveouts and shall not constitute a Material Adverse Impact.

Answer the question by selecting the correct option.
